Now question 3c: Last login time of Spectre using the timezone found in 2 (Singapore). The last login time is stored in the SAM hive in the F value of the user. The F value contains the last login time at offset 0x08 (8 bytes FILETIME). Let me parse it.

The F value structure:
- offset 0x08: last login time (FILETIME, 8 bytes)
- offset 0x18: last password set
- offset 0x20: account expires
- offset 0x28: last password failure

Let me write a script to extract the last login time and convert to Singapore time.

2026-10-08 21:20:22,093 INFO 🎬 ACTION (primary)
edit 1:20
from Registry import Registry
import struct, datetime

reg = Registry.Registry("extracted/SAM")
users = reg.open("SAM\\Domains\\Account\\Users")
# find RID 1001
for sub in users.subkeys():
    if sub.name() == "Names":
        continue
    if sub.name().endswith("1001"):
        f = sub.value("F").value()
        last_login = struct.unpack("<Q", f[0x08:0x10])[0]
        # FILETIME to datetime
        dt = datetime.datetime(1601,1,1) + datetime.timedelta(microseconds=last_login/10)
        print("UTC:", dt)
        # Singapore is UTC+8
        sg = dt + datetime.timedelta(hours=8)
